--- serving files
/ is index.html: 200 true text/html; charset=utf-8
and its length is the file's: true
/index.html: 200 true
/css/site.css 200 text/css; charset=utf-8 true true
/img/logo.png 200 image/png true true
/data.json 200 application/json true true
/LOUD.HTML 200 text/html; charset=utf-8 true true
/blob.bin 200 application/octet-stream true true
/README 200 application/octet-stream true true
/big.js 200 text/javascript; charset=utf-8 true true
every octet of a binary file survives: true
a percent-encoded name: b'spaced\n' b'utf-8 name\n'
the query string is not part of the path: 200
empty segments are dropped: 200
--- directories
/docs/ serves its index.html: true
/docs is a 301 to /docs/: true /docs/
a directory with no index.html is a 404: 404 text/plain; charset=utf-8 b'not found\n'
a missing file is a 404: 404 404
--- methods
HEAD has the GET's length and no body: 200 14 text/html; charset=utf-8
and the next response on the connection starts where HEAD's head ended: 200 200000 200 b'body { color: black }\n'
POST -> 405 GET, HEAD b'method not allowed\n'
PUT -> 405 GET, HEAD b'method not allowed\n'
DELETE -> 405 GET, HEAD b'method not allowed\n'
OPTIONS -> 405 GET, HEAD b'method not allowed\n'
--- with a router in front
a routed path goes to the router: b'ok\n'
and a routed path's 405 is the router's, not the files': 405 POST
everything else goes to the files: 200 404
--- traversal
/../secret.txt -> 400
/css/../../secret.txt -> 400
/.. -> 400
/css/.. -> 400
/%2e%2e/secret.txt -> 400
/%2E%2E/secret.txt -> 400
/.%2e/secret.txt -> 400
/%2e./secret.txt -> 400
/css/..%2f..%2fsecret.txt -> 400
/css%2f..%2f..%2fsecret.txt -> 400
/%2e%2e%2fsecret.txt -> 400
--- decoded once, not twice
/%252e%252e/secret.txt -> 404 (a name, not a climb)
/%252e%252e/decoded-once.txt -> 200 (the directory literally named %2e%2e)
--- NUL
/index.html%00 -> 400
/index.html%00.png -> 400
/%00 -> 400
/css/%00/../secret.txt -> 400
--- backslash
/..%5csecret.txt -> 400
/css%5c..%5c..%5csecret.txt -> 400
/..\secret.txt -> 400
/css\site.css -> 400
--- absolute paths
//<the secret's absolute path> -> 404
//etc/passwd -> 404
/etc/passwd -> 404
absolute-form, climbing -> 400
absolute-form, absolute -> 404
--- encodings the parser refuses first
an overlong UTF-8 dot, %c0%ae%c0%ae -> 400 b'bytes could not be decoded as UTF-8: invalid byte 0xc0 at position 1\n'
a malformed escape, %2 -> 400 b'invalid percent-escape in the request target\n'
and the handler's own refusal, for comparison -> b'bad path\n'
--- symlinks are resolved, not trusted
a file link pointing outside the root -> 403 false
a directory link pointing outside the root -> 403 false
a link that stays inside the root is served -> 200 text/css; charset=utf-8
--- a hand-built Request
'secret.txt' -> 400
'*' -> 400
'' -> 400
'/../secret.txt' -> 400
'/a\x00b' -> 400
'/a\\b' -> 400
the bad-path answer says so: bad path

--- file_response
200 text/css; charset=utf-8 22 b'body { color: black }\n'
a custom 404 page: 404 text/html; charset=utf-8 <h1>custom not found</h1>

a missing file: 404 not found

a directory: 404
--- static_files refuses a root it cannot serve
ValueError: static_files() root '' is not a directory
ValueError: static_files() root '<root>/nope' is not a directory
ValueError: static_files() root '<root>/index.html' is not a directory
static_files() root must be str, not <class 'int'>
file_response() path must be str, not <class 'bytes'>
--- http.fetch agrees
200 text/javascript; charset=utf-8 200000 true
200000
nothing was forced at shutdown: true
cleaned up: true
